	quest.0000000000013C19.title: "Apotheosis Enchanting"
	quest.0000000000013C4C.quest_desc: [
		"Craft the Apothic Enchanting Library and consult its guide for storing and using enchanted books. This block is not an infusion altar."
		"Next routes: Legendary Gear. These are the quests that directly use this step; other prerequisites may also apply."
	]
	quest.0000000000013C4C.title: "Enchanting Library"
	quest.0000000000013C90.quest_desc: [
		"Build a beacon from a nether star and glass. Place it on a pyramid for powerful permanent buffs."
		"Next routes: Ascension. These are the quests that directly use this step; other prerequisites may also apply."
	]
	quest.0000000000013C90.title: "Beacon"
	quest.0000000000013CD4.quest_desc: [
		"Obtain a Nether Star. A normal survival route is four soul sand and three Wither Skeleton skulls from the Nether, then summon and defeat a Wither in a safe arena. This comes before the Beacon quest, since a beacon consumes a star."
		"Next routes: Beacon. These are the quests that directly use this step; other prerequisites may also apply."
	]
	quest.0000000000013CD4.title: "A Nether Star"
	quest.0000000000013D18.quest_desc: [
		"Complete the vanilla Free the End advancement by defeating the dragon. A dragon egg is not required, so another team taking the first egg cannot block your campaign. If the dragon is already dead, place four End Crystals around the exit portal to respawn it."
		"Next routes: Wings of Freedom; Ascension. These are the quests that directly use this step; other prerequisites may also apply."
	]
	quest.0000000000013D18.title: "Defeat the Ender Dragon"
	quest.0000000000013D5C.quest_desc: [
		"Elytra give you true flight. Combine with rockets for infinite speed across the void."
		"Next routes: Ascension. These are the quests that directly use this step; other prerequisites may also apply."
	]
	quest.0000000000013D5C.title: "Wings of Freedom"
	quest.0000000000013D8F.quest_desc: [
		"Socket legendary gems into your gear for the absolute best stats possible."
		"Next routes: Fully Automated. These are the quests that directly use this step; other prerequisites may also apply."
	]
	quest.0000000000013D8F.title: "Legendary Gear"
	quest.0000000000013DD3.quest_desc: [
		"Your reactor and turbine generate more RF than everything in your base combined can consume."
		"Next routes: Fully Automated; Ascension. These are the quests that directly use this step; other prerequisites may also apply."
	]
	quest.0000000000013DD3.title: "Infinite Power"
	quest.0000000000013E28.quest_desc: [
		"Your AE2 network auto-crafts everything, the induction matrix stores it all, and spirits mine the rest."
		"Next routes: Ascension. These are the quests that directly use this step; other prerequisites may also apply."
	]
	quest.0000000000013E28.title: "Fully Automated"
	quest.0000000000013EB0.quest_desc: [
		"You started with a single tree and a handful of dirt suspended in an endless sky.\n\nYou've built machines that reshape matter, woven spells into steel, harnessed the power of stars, and forged something that has never existed before.\n\nThis is what you came here to build.\n\nThe sky was never the limit — it was the beginning."
		"This is the final pack milestone. Your island remains available for further building and automation."
	]
	quest.0000000000013EB0.quest_subtitle: "The sky was never the limit."
	quest.0000000000013EB0.title: "Ascension"
	quest.710000000000001B.quest_desc: [
		"Craft any Ex Deorum wooden water crucible. Oak, spruce, birch and the other registered wood variants count. Feed surplus saplings for water: ten saplings make one bucket; leaves also work if you can collect them. Porcelain crucibles make lava instead and do not satisfy this task."
		"Next routes: Build a Renewable Water Pool. These are the quests that directly use this step; other prerequisites may also apply."
	]
	quest.710000000000001B.title: "Water from Saplings"
	quest.710000000000001D.quest_desc: [
		"Crook ordinary leaves until a silkworm drops. Use it on leaves, wait for infestation to spread fully, then crook the infested leaves for string. Keep ordinary trees as well as an infested tree."
		"Next routes: A Quick Snack; Weave a String Mesh. These are the quests that directly use this step; other prerequisites may also apply."
	]
	quest.710000000000001D.title: "Silkworms and String"
	quest.710000000000001F.quest_desc: [
		"Smelt spare silkworms into Cooked Silkworms while your wheat grows. Keep one silkworm for infesting another tree. This is an optional early food source, not a replacement for a renewable farm."
		"This optional branch ends here. Return to the chapter route and continue a square quest or work toward its hexagonal checkpoint."
	]
	quest.710000000000001F.title: "A Quick Snack"
	quest.7100000000000021.quest_desc: [
		"Build a 2 by 2 pool with a solid floor. Place water sources in opposite corners. Take a bucket from a corner and check that the water reforms. You can obtain a second source from the nearby sand island's ice or your oak crucible. Tick this only after testing your pool; this is a manual build check."
		"Next routes: Opening Supplies Ready; Dust and Water Make Clay. These are the quests that directly use this step; other prerequisites may also apply."
	]
	quest.7100000000000021.title: "Build a Renewable Water Pool"
	quest.7100000000000023.quest_desc: [
		"Collect four staple foods. Bread, baked potatoes, carrots, apples, cooked meat/fish, cooked silkworms and the listed rice dishes all count. Establish a renewable supply; keep seeds or breeding stock instead of eating your last starter resource."
		"Next routes: Opening Supplies Ready. These are the quests that directly use this step; other prerequisites may also apply."
	]
	quest.7100000000000023.title: "Food Before Bigger Machines"
	quest.7100000000000027.quest_desc: [
		"Hold the listed supplies after establishing your water pool and food patch. The item tasks check supplies, while the previous manual water check covers the pool. Continue into powered resource automation when these basics are reliable."
		"Next routes: A Small Powered Workshop. These are the quests that directly use this step; other prerequisites may also apply."
	]
	quest.7100000000000027.title: "Opening Supplies Ready"
	quest.7100000000000041.quest_desc: [
		"Sieve gravel using a string or flint mesh until you have four Ex Deorum iron ore chunks. The bundled chance is 10% with string and 12% with flint. This is a random drop: keep a renewable gravel supply."
		"Next routes: Chunks into Smeltable Ore. These are the quests that directly use this step; other prerequisites may also apply."
	]
	quest.7100000000000041.title: "Ore Chunks from Gravel"
	quest.7100000000000043.quest_desc: [
		"Craft four iron ore chunks in a 2 by 2 pattern to obtain one iron ore block, then smelt it for an ingot. Repeat until you can afford buckets, shears and hoppers."
		"Next routes: First Iron Ingots. These are the quests that directly use this step; other prerequisites may also apply."
	]
	quest.7100000000000043.title: "Chunks into Smeltable Ore"
	quest.7100000000000045.quest_desc: [
		"Sieve dust with your string or flint mesh for bone meal. Reserve seven bone meal for the porcelain-clay route before using it all on crops. Bone meal also helps you recover grass and additional seeds."
		"Next routes: Porcelain Clay. These are the quests that directly use this step; other prerequisites may also apply."
	]
	quest.7100000000000045.title: "Bone Meal from Dust"
	quest.7100000000000047.quest_desc: [
		"Fill an empty oak barrel with water, then add Ex Deorum dust to make a clay block. Break the block into clay balls. Use your renewable pool once buckets are available, or collect rain."
		"Next routes: Porcelain Clay; Dielectric Casing. These are the quests that directly use this step; other prerequisites may also apply."
		"From other chapters: Build a Renewable Water Pool (Skyblock Basics)."
	]
	quest.7100000000000047.title: "Dust and Water Make Clay"
	quest.7100000000000049.quest_desc: [
		"Combine clay balls and bone meal, one of each per porcelain clay ball. Seven porcelain clay balls make an unfired crucible."
		"Next routes: Shape the Crucible. These are the quests that directly use this step; other prerequisites may also apply."
	]
	quest.7100000000000049.title: "Porcelain Clay"
	quest.710000000000004B.quest_desc: [
		"Use seven porcelain clay balls in the bucket-shaped crucible pattern shown by JEI. This is not yet a working crucible: smelt it next."
		"Next routes: Fire the Porcelain Crucible. These are the quests that directly use this step; other prerequisites may also apply."
	]
	quest.710000000000004B.title: "Shape the Crucible"
	quest.710000000000004D.quest_desc: [
		"Craft a Starter Furnator. Its dielectric paste uses charcoal/coal, clay balls and lava; establish renewable lava first. Feed the generator charcoal. This starter tier is enough to begin the small machines below."
		"Next routes: Your First Mechanical Sieve; First Generator. These are the quests that directly use this step; other prerequisites may also apply."
		"From other chapters: Dielectric Casing (Power Energy); Opening Supplies Ready (Skyblock Basics)."
	]
	quest.710000000000004D.title: "A Small Powered Workshop"
	quest.710000000000004F.quest_desc: [
		"Craft an Ex Deorum mechanical sieve. This update replaces only the two iron-block ingredients with iron ingots to shorten the opening grind. Keep an appropriate mesh in the machine, give it FE, and feed gravel."
		"Next routes: Feed the Line; Watch One Batch Run. These are the quests that directly use this step; other prerequisites may also apply."
	]
	quest.710000000000004F.title: "Your First Mechanical Sieve"
	quest.7100000000000051.quest_desc: [
		"Craft an Ex Deorum mechanical hammer. Place it beside a powered supply and use hoppers to feed and collect the right material. Its two iron-block ingredients are also reduced to iron ingots. Inspect the hammer recipe chain in JEI before routing outputs."
		"This optional branch ends here. Return to the chapter route and continue a square quest or work toward its hexagonal checkpoint."
	]
	quest.7100000000000051.title: "Feed the Line"
	quest.7100000000000053.quest_desc: [
		"Manual operating check: fuel the Starter Furnator, power the mechanical sieve (direct adjacency or suitable Powah cable), insert its mesh, feed a stack of gravel, and route outputs into a chest. Confirm that it processes without repeated hand-sieving. If it stops, check fuel/FE, the mesh, sided input and output space. Tick after watching a batch run."
		"This optional branch ends here. Return to the chapter route and continue a square quest or work toward its hexagonal checkpoint."
	]
	quest.7100000000000053.title: "Watch One Batch Run"
	quest.7100000000000057.quest_desc: [
		"Craft Manaforged Alloy from Forged Cores, Ars source gems and infused alloy. Make the Infuser and establish an Ars source-gem route first. The Enrichment Chamber needs four of these alloys; this update keeps that existing recipe cost."
		"Next routes: Enrichment Chamber; Forge the Sky Core. These are the quests that directly use this step; other prerequisites may also apply."
		"From other chapters: Source Gems First (Ars Nouveau)."
	]
	quest.7100000000000057.title: "Manaforged Alloy"
	quest.7100000000000059.quest_desc: [
		"Build and operate the IE coke oven and blast furnace using the Engineer's Manual. Obtain steel for the Forged Core. JEI shows the bricks and components; a hammer alone is not proof of steel production."
		"Next routes: IE Crusher; Forge the Connection. These are the quests that directly use this step; other prerequisites may also apply."
	]
	quest.7100000000000059.title: "Steel Before Circuits"
	task.000000000000FA02.title: "I've set up my team!"
	quest.7300000000000001.title: "A Route to the Nether"
	quest.7300000000000001.quest_desc: [
		"The sand island 75 blocks north contains ten obsidian. Build and light a normal Nether portal; keep a safe way home. The Nether uses normal terrain, including fortresses. Bring food, blocks and spare ignition tools. Tick this after testing travel."
		"Next routes: Heated Brass; Prosperity in the Void; Build an End Portal. These are the quests that directly use this step; other prerequisites may also apply."
	]
	quest.7300000000000003.title: "Archwood from Moss"
	quest.7300000000000003.quest_desc: [
		"Sieve dirt for Ex Deorum grass seeds, then craft four grass seeds into a moss block. Sieve moss to obtain an Ars archwood sapling; the installed Ex Deorum recipes support the four archwood colours. Grow it for archwood planks and slabs."
		"Next routes: Source Jars; Source Gems First. These are the quests that directly use this step; other prerequisites may also apply."
		"From other chapters: Flint Mesh (Ex Nihilo)."
	]
	quest.7300000000000005.title: "Prosperity in the Void"
	quest.7300000000000005.quest_desc: [
		"This update adds a deterministic prosperity-shard recipe: four amethyst shards, four Nether quartz and one gold ingot make four prosperity shards. Obtain quartz in the normal Nether; use JEI for amethyst acquisition. Inferium can drop from mobs before you craft its seeds."
		"Next routes: Inferium Seeds. These are the quests that directly use this step; other prerequisites may also apply."
		"From other chapters: A Route to the Nether (Ex Nihilo)."
	]
	quest.7300000000000007.title: "Build an End Portal"
	quest.7300000000000007.quest_desc: [
		"The void Overworld has no stronghold route. Craft twelve End Portal Frames using the added recipe: each batch of four obsidian, four Eyes of Ender and one diamond makes three frames. Keep twelve additional Eyes to activate them. Stand in the centre of a 5 by 5 area and place the twelve frames around a 3 by 3 opening, facing inward; leave corners empty. Check orientation before adding Eyes."
		"Next routes: Defeat the Ender Dragon. These are the quests that directly use this step; other prerequisites may also apply."
		"From other chapters: A Route to the Nether (Ex Nihilo); Diamond in the Rough (Ex Nihilo)."
	]
	quest.0000000000010F24.quest_subtitle: "Branch checkpoint - follow your chosen route"
	quest.0000000000011463.quest_subtitle: "Branch checkpoint - follow your chosen route"
	quest.0000000000011980.quest_subtitle: "Branch checkpoint - follow your chosen route"
	quest.0000000000011E7B.quest_subtitle: "Branch checkpoint - follow your chosen route"
	quest.00000000000123CB.quest_subtitle: "Branch checkpoint - follow your chosen route"
	quest.000000000001291B.quest_subtitle: "Branch checkpoint - follow your chosen route"
	quest.0000000000012E8D.quest_subtitle: "Branch checkpoint - follow your chosen route"
	quest.00000000000133CC.quest_subtitle: "Branch checkpoint - follow your chosen route"
	quest.000000000001393E.quest_subtitle: "Branch checkpoint - follow your chosen route"
	quest.7300000000000009.title: "A Workshop Achievement"
	quest.7300000000000009.quest_desc: [
		"Complete one specialist chapter checkpoint: power, Create, Mekanism, storage, Ars, Occultism, renewable production, IE or automation. Your chosen branch feeds into Ascension; the other specialisations remain optional. Tick this after completing one checkpoint."
		"Workshop checkpoint: complete any one of the listed prerequisite quests, then satisfy this quest's own tasks. You do not need every branch."
		"Next routes: Ascension. These are the quests that directly use this step; other prerequisites may also apply."
		"From other chapters: Power Broker (Power Energy); Fully Automated (Create); Mekanism Mastery (Mekanism); Autocrafting Route Established (Storage); The Archmage (Ars Nouveau); Master of Spirits (Occultism); Renewable Production Established (Farming Food); Industrial Revolution (Immersive Engineering); Automation Route Established (Cross Mod Automation)."
	]
	quest.730000000000000B.title: "Forge the Sky Core"
	quest.730000000000000B.quest_desc: [
		"Craft the pack's Sky Core. JEI shows its Manaforged Alloys, precision mechanisms, electronic components and reinforced alloy. This joins Create, steel, Ars and Mekanism into the campaign; the workshop checkpoint lets you choose your additional specialisation."
		"Next routes: Ascension. These are the quests that directly use this step; other prerequisites may also apply."
		"From other chapters: Manaforged Alloy (Mekanism); Reinforced Alloy (Mekanism); Forge the Connection (Cross Mod Automation)."
	]
